; Example usage of the `dimensions` plugin. Every value here validates.
;
; `:dimension` and `:view` both hold digit-leading spellings, written
; exactly as the WebGPU spec writes them: no lookup table, no quoting.
;
;   * `2d` is the member `2d`.
;   * `2.0d` and `02d` are the *same* member: matching is on the parsed
;     `(magnitude, unit)` pair, so an incidental spelling still resolves.
;   * `cube` is an ordinary symbol member in the same set.
;   * `2d-array` is one token: inside a unit, a `-` joins two letter runs
;     when the next byte is a letter. `1em-2` is still `1em` then `-2`.
;
; What would not validate: `4d` (not declared, so `not_member`, naming the
; set), `2.5d` (fractional magnitudes match nothing), and a bare `2` (no
; unit, so not a spelling at all, so `wrong_underlying`).

(texture :name albedo    :dimension 2d   :view 2d)
(texture :name lightmap  :dimension 2.0d :view cube)
(texture :name volume    :dimension 3d)
(texture :name shadow    :dimension 02d  :view cube-array)
(texture :name gradient  :dimension 1d   :view 1d)
(texture :name atlas     :dimension 2d   :view 2d-array)
